Fri Oct 23 17:39:49 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 4.2:
  * Move udev rules/hwdb from 80- to 70- prefix so the power button
    keeps working with systemd v258 in gamescope-session
  * Support ASUS ROG Xbox Ally and Xbox Ally X, ZOTAC Gaming Zone Pro;
    fix Legion Go 2 long-press mapping and cover its BIOS variants
  * Detect devices by key presence instead of an explicit list, track
    META+F16, support lid switch, SIGHUP reload, node blacklisting,
    raise max devices from 2 to 10
  * Fix short-press key-repeat handling and long-press detection
    after suspend/resume by re-enumerating stale device FDs
  * Switch _service to official upstream
    (gitlab.steamos.cloud/holo/powerbuttond); the previous mirror
    carries no tags past 3.3
- Drop fix-cmdline-overflow.patch: upstream bounded the device loop
  by MAX_DEVS, so the downstream argument guard is redundant

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Oct 20 11:13:55 UTC 2025 - Matthias Gerstner <matthias.gerstner@suse.com>

- add fix-cmdline-overflow.patch: this fixes memory corruption if more than
  MAX_DEVS command line arguments are passed.

  An invocation like:

  /usr/lib/hwsupport/steamos-powerbuttond /dev/input/event0 /dev/input/event1 /dev/input/event2 /dev/input/event3 /dev/input/event4 /dev/input/event5 /dev/input/event0

  otherwise ends up in a segmentation fault or similar issues.

  Finding in the context of the review bug bsc#1249602.

  The upstream repository is only a mirror from semi-public Valve sources, so
  submitting it there doesn't seem to make sense at the moment.

